5,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,I think we should look at the incident logs and the time lost to copying records.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,May,,I’m curious about the staffing of the coordination group and how vendor queries are handled.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,I want to check network coverage at customer plants and in-house developer availability.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I’ll examine the capital budget and software allowance, plus the vendor licence pricing versus fixed-fee work.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I’d like to see the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, do you think the coordination group’s workload will affect how we judge these proposals?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, absolutely. If the same two people are drowning, any new tool that adds to their plate is a non-starter.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, if the capital line is frozen, does that kill any proposal needing new hardware, or is it just a delay?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, it’s not a delay. The capital line is frozen, so any proposal requiring new hardware is effectively dead on arrival.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, that’s a hard constraint. Does that mean we should only consider software-only solutions for this round?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, I’m not sure. We need to see if the existing infrastructure can support the new tools without extra hardware.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,May,,"@Kenji, hardware isn’t the only trap. If a tool demands constant manual updates, we’re just hiring ghosts to do the work.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, fair point. But if the groundwork is missing, we’re just promising dates we can’t keep.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, agreed. But remember, the recurring software allowance still has room. We can fund the subscription without touching the frozen capital line.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, that’s a relief. So we can fund the subscription, but we still need to ensure the groundwork is solid before we commit.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, I worry that if we ignore the daily losses, we’ll just pick another impressive-sounding tool that fails on the floor.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, exactly. We need to see if the daily effort actually drops, not just if the demo looks slick.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Daisuke, agreed. We must verify the technical groundwork before promising anything.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Kenji, let’s keep the recurring costs in mind. The frozen capital line means we must rely on the software allowance, so affordability is the real test.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, noted. I’ll keep the recurring costs in mind, but I’m still waiting to see if these tools actually survive their first year.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
