35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, the incident logs show eleven misrouted deliveries this year, all traced to duplicate addresses.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, that’s a clear win for a shared catalog. But my staffing check shows the coordination group is still running on two people","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, the network checks are grim. Half the customer sites lose signal for whole afternoons. A mobile app is useless there.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, that confirms the hardware risk. But the recurring software allowance still has room, so we can fund the subscription without touching the frozen capital line.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, that’s a critical flaw. If the app can’t sync offline, it’s just a digital clipboard. I’m worried about the daily entry burden","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, the timing data is worse. We lose nearly an hour daily just copying details that already exist elsewhere.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, that hour is pure waste. My vendor query check shows clerks re-requesting the same certificates yearly. A shared hub would stop that bleeding.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, the developer situation is worse. Both are locked into the accounting upgrade until Q3, and the previous integrator left the interfaces undocumented.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, that’s a major bottleneck. If we can’t build or maintain it internally, we’re stuck relying on expensive external fixed-fee work, which is the only stable pricing option left.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, that’s a red flag. If the groundwork is missing, we’re just promising dates we can’t keep.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, that hour of copying is exactly the kind of daily loss we need to fix. Does the shared hub actually reduce that manual effort?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, yes. Consolidating the records means we stop re-entering the same data. It directly attacks that daily hour of waste.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, with developers locked until Q3 and undocumented interfaces, any build-heavy proposal is a gamble. We need something that doesn’t require new code.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, agreed. We must avoid heavy builds. The fixed-fee work is stable, but we still need to ensure the recurring costs fit within the software allowance.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, I found that tools needing daily entry from everyone were quietly dropped. We must pick something narrow that one trade actually uses, or it dies.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, that’s the pattern I feared. If it’s not narrow and useful, it dies. We need a tool that survives its first year","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Kenji, exactly. And my staffing check confirms the coordination group is drowning. We can’t add another tool that demands constant manual updates from those two people.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, that pattern is exactly why I’m wary. If the groundwork is missing, we’re just promising dates we can’t keep.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Kenji, agreed. The pattern is clear. We need a narrow, low-maintenance tool that fits the recurring allowance, not a heavy build that dies in year one.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, agreed. But I also found that cross-unit standardization efforts often fail without a clear owner. We need to ensure whoever we pick has a dedicated champion, or it will vanish like the others.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
