60,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, the candidates are out. Given the network issues and the need to stop copying records, does the Supplier Data Hub look like the safest bet?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, it’s the only one that doesn’t need new hardware or constant manual updates. It fixes the duplicate address problem directly.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Daisuke, agreed. It’s a data consolidation, not a build. No new code, no network dependency. It fits the constraints we’ve established.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, precisely. It avoids the frozen capital line and the developer bottleneck. The recurring cost fits our allowance, making it the only financially viable option.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, agreed. But remember my finding: standardization fails without an owner. We must assign a dedicated champion for the Hub, or it will vanish like the others.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, that’s the missing piece. If we don’t name a specific person to own it, we’re just repeating the same mistake. Who do we trust to keep it alive?","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, I’d nominate the lead clerk from the planning office. They already handle the vendor queries and know the data pain points intimately.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, that’s a solid pick. They’re already in the weeds. But I need to know: does the Hub require any new interfaces, or is it purely data consolidation?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, it’s purely consolidation. No new interfaces, just merging existing records. The fixed-fee setup keeps costs predictable within our allowance.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, correct. It’s purely consolidation. No new code, just merging existing records. The fixed-fee setup keeps costs predictable within our allowance.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, if the lead clerk owns it, does that add to their already heavy workload? We can’t just shift the burden without checking capacity.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, it’s a trade-off. They lose the re-entry drudgery, gaining time. It’s a net win, not a burden.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, fair point. But if the groundwork is missing, we’re just promising dates we can’t keep.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the groundwork is the existing records. We are consolidating what is already there, not building new infrastructure. The risk is low.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, agreed. The groundwork exists. We just need a dedicated owner to prevent it from becoming another abandoned standardization effort.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, that makes sense. If it saves them an hour daily, it’s a relief, not a burden. I’m ready to vote for the Hub.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, agreed. It’s the only option that respects our staffing limits and budget. I’m voting for the Supplier Data Hub.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Daisuke, agreed. It’s the only candidate that doesn’t require new code or network access. I’m voting for the Supplier Data Hub.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, agreed. It fits the recurring allowance without touching the frozen capital line. I’m voting for the Supplier Data Hub.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Daisuke, agreed. It’s the only one with a clear owner and a proven pattern of survival. I’m voting for the Supplier Data Hub.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
